      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the middle-aged man in <Picture 1> with grey hair, headphones hanging around his neck, and a grey shirt and dark jeans.\n<Subject 2> is the man in <Picture 2> with brown hair, a short brown beard, headhpones, a green shirt, and dark jeans.\n<Subject 3> is the professional soundstage shown in <Picture 3> with miscellaneous equipment, microphones, and a computer cart. \n<Audio 1> is a predefined audio track and is reused in the target video.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reuse] The target video is synced to the sound of <Audio 1>. It shows <Subject 1> using a clapboard to start a scene in <Subject 3> with <Subject 2> behind him.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - the man's grey hair, headphones around his neck, and grey shirt and jeans are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - the man's brown hair, headhpones, green shirt, and dark jeans are retained.\n<Subject 3> (location for [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - the location serves as a backdrop for the action and is retained.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - <Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is live-action cinematic realism in a working-documentary style, slightly underexposed and slightly desaturated.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot establishes <Subject 3> and opens on <Subject 1> holding an open clapboard. <Subject 2> has his right hand on the mock door-frame equipment seen in <Subject 3> and is behind <Subject 1>. From out of frame we hear a voice from <Audio 1> say <d>[English] Quiet, please.</d>. Perfectly synchronized with the clapboard clack from <Audio 1>, the <Subject 1> claps the clapboard in a swift fluid motion. After the clap <Subject 1> holds position with the clapboard closed.\n\noverall_soundscape:\n<Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track, including its soundstage room tone, spoken cue, and clapboard crack.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "value": "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the middle-aged man in <Picture 1> with grey hair, headphones hanging around his neck, and a grey shirt and dark jeans.\n<Subject 2> is the man in <Picture 2> with brown hair, a short brown beard, headhpones, a green shirt, and dark jeans.\n<Subject 3> is the professional soundstage shown in <Picture 3> with miscellaneous equipment, microphones, and a computer cart. \n<Audio 1> is a predefined audio track and is reused in the target video.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation + audio reuse] The target video is synced to the sound of <Audio 1>. It shows <Subject 1> using a clapboard to start a scene in <Subject 3> with <Subject 2> behind him.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - the man's grey hair, headphones around his neck, and grey shirt and jeans are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - the man's brown hair, headhpones, green shirt, and dark jeans are retained.\n<Subject 3> (location for [Shot 1]): partially_preserved - the location serves as a backdrop for the action and is retained.\n<Audio 1>: fully_copy - <Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is live-action cinematic realism in a working-documentary style, slightly underexposed and slightly desaturated.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot establishes <Subject 3> and opens on <Subject 1> holding an open clapboard. <Subject 2> has his right hand on the mock door-frame equipment seen in <Subject 3> and is behind <Subject 1>. From out of frame we hear a voice from <Audio 1> say <d>[English] Quiet, please.</d>. Perfectly synchronized with the clapboard clack from <Audio 1>, the <Subject 1> claps the clapboard in a swift fluid motion. After the clap <Subject 1> holds position with the clapboard closed.\n\noverall_soundscape:\n<Audio 1> is reused 1:1 as the target video's complete final audio track, including its soundstage